#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:3
msgid "Use a private index"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:5
msgid ""
"Install from a private index, behind a proxy, or offline by forwarding index "
"options to the backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:9
msgid "Set the index for one command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:11
msgid ""
"Pass ``--index-url`` directly, or forward pip options with ``--pip-args``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:13
msgid ""
"$ pipx install my-package --index-url https://my-index.example.com/simple/\n"
"$ pipx install my-package --pip-args=\"--extra-index-url https://my-index."
"example.com/simple/\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:18
msgid ""
"Quote ``--pip-args`` and use an ``=`` sign so pipx passes the whole string "
"through. Add trusted hosts and other pip flags the same way:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:21
msgid ""
"$ pipx install my-package --pip-args=\"--index-url https://my-index.example."
"com/simple/ --trusted-host my-index.example.com\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:27
msgid "Set it for every command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:29
msgid ""
"pipx forwards ``PIP_*`` environment variables to every pip invocation, "
"including shared-library upgrades. Set them in your shell profile or pip's "
"own config file for a permanent default:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:32
msgid ""
"$ export PIP_INDEX_URL=https://my-index.example.com/simple/\n"
"$ export PIP_TRUSTED_HOST=my-index.example.com\n"
"$ pipx install my-private-package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:38
msgid ""
"See the `pip configuration docs <https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/topics/"
"configuration/>`_ for the config-file form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:42
msgid "Install offline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:44
msgid ""
"Point pip at a local directory of wheels and stop it reaching the network:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:46
msgid ""
"$ pipx install my-package --pip-args=\"--no-index --find-links /path/to/"
"wheels\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:50
msgid ""
"Pass ``--skip-maintenance`` to keep the bundled pip instead of downloading a "
"shared-library upgrade during the install."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:54
msgid ""
"Under the uv backend, pipx translates only a subset of ``--pip-args``: ``--"
"index-url`` (``-i``), ``--extra-index-url``, ``--find-links`` (``-f``), ``--"
"trusted-host``, ``--no-binary``, ``--only-binary``, ``--pre``, ``--upgrade`` "
"(``-U``), and ``--no-cache-dir``. Any other flag raises an error rather than "
"being silently dropped. Use ``--backend pip`` when you need a flag uv cannot "
"translate. See :doc:`use-uv-backend`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:61
msgid "Verify it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:63
msgid "$ pipx list --short"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-private-index.rst:67
msgid ""
"The package installs at the version your index serves. For a private index "
"that pipx must also use for its own shared libraries, set the ``PIP_*`` "
"variables before the first install."
msgstr ""
